  "result": "I fixed all three problems in `src/queue.js`, and `npm test` now passes (5 of 5 tests).\n\n- **Hang after a failure:** a rejected job never freed its slot, so the queue stalled. A job that threw synchronously also never freed its slot. Both now release the slot, and the failure rejects only that job's own promise.\n- **`onIdle()` resolving early:** it only checked that nothing was pending. It now also waits until nothing is running.\n- **One job at a time after `resume()`:** `next()` started only one job per call. It now loops until the concurrency limit is reached, so `resume()` fills every free slot.\n\nI added three regression tests to `test/queue.test.js`:\n- The queue keeps going after a job rejects or throws synchronously.\n- `onIdle()` waits for running jobs even when nothing is pending.\n- With concurrency 4, `resume()` starts four jobs at once, and the peak never exceeds four.\n\nI did not run the new tests against the old code, so I haven't confirmed that each one fails without the fix.",
